Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: catalog.c
Line: 1093
Function: xmlCatalogNormalizePublic
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: ret is assigned the result of xmlStrdup(pubID) without checking for allocation failure. If xmlStrdup returns NULL, subsequent writes via q (which equals ret) such as '*q = 0' will dereference a NULL pointer, causing a crash.

